</style></head><body><header><div class="eyebrow">The freezer cube collection · v1.0</div><h1>Southwest, by the cube.</h1><p>Four fully cooked recipes designed to freeze separately in silicone molds, then combine into whatever meal you want. Search, scale, portion, and build your macros.</p></header><main><div class="toolbar"><input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Search recipes, ingredients, tags or techniques…" aria-label="Search recipes"><select id="filter"><option value="all">All recipes</option><option value="protein">Protein</option><option value="starch">Rice & starch</option><option value="beans">Beans</option><option value="vegetable">Vegetables</option></select><button id="print" onclick="window.print()">Print recipes</button><button id="reset" onclick="resetAll()">Reset portions</button></div><div id="cards" class="cards"></div><div id="empty">No recipes found. Try another ingredient or category.</div><section class="builder" id="builder"><div class="category">Mix & match</div><h2>Build a meal from frozen cubes</h2><p class="sub">Select the number of finished cubes you plan to combine. Values use the estimated macros per cube below.</p><div id="builderItems" class="builder-grid"></div><div id="total" class="total"></div><p class="disclaimer">Estimates only: cube macros depend on actual cooked yield, can labels, ingredient brands and how evenly sauce and solids are divided. One cup is a volume measure, not a fixed weight. Measure your finished yield before filling molds for more accurate results.</p></section><div class="footer">Food safety: cook chicken to 165°F (74°C); refrigerate cooked food promptly in shallow containers, especially rice, and freeze once chilled. Reheat leftovers thoroughly to 165°F. Photos are illustrative examples from third-party food sites, not photographs of these exact recipes. Images require an internet connection. Source links and credits appear on each card. Nutritional figures are planning estimates, not verified lab values. <a href="https://www.fsis.usda.gov/food-safety/safe-food-handling-and-preparation/food-safety-basics/leftovers-and-food-safety">USDA leftover guidance</a> · <a href="https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/">USDA FoodData Central</a>.</div></main><script>
const recipes=[
{id:'chicken',type:'protein',name:'Creamy Chipotle Chicken',tag:'Smoky · creamy · high protein',desc:'Tender shredded chicken breast in a bold adobo sauce, enriched with light cream cheese and Greek yogurt.',photo:'https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/61126f988b287208e9da25ea/2118edae-8250-4bb6-b7e8-33a3d55e24d4/Slow%2BCooker%2BCreamy%2BChipotle%2BRanch%2BShredded%2BChicken.png',credit:'Chompions · illustrative',source:'https://www.chompions.com/all-recipes/slow-cooker-creamy-chipotle-ranch-shredded-chicken',time:'40–50 min',yield:6,unit:'1 cup',mac:{cal:260,p:34,c:8,f:9},ingredients:[['2','lb','boneless skinless chicken breast'],['1','tsp','kosher salt (adjust to taste)'],['1','tsp','smoked paprika'],['1','tsp','ground cumin (chicken)'],['0.5','tsp','black pepper'],['2','tsp','avocado oil'],['3','','chipotle peppers in adobo'],['1','tbsp','adobo sauce'],['4','oz','reduced-fat cream cheese'],['0.75','cup','low-sodium chicken broth'],['0.5','cup','plain nonfat Greek yogurt'],['3','','garlic cloves, minced'],['1','tsp','ground cumin (sauce)'],['0.5','tsp','dried oregano'],['1','tbsp','lime juice'],['0.5','tsp','MSG (optional)']],steps:['Cut chicken into large pieces and season with salt, smoked paprika, cumin and pepper.','Heat avocado oil in a wide pan and briefly sear chicken to develop color; do not cook it through yet.','Blend chipotles, adobo sauce, broth, garlic, sauce cumin and oregano until smooth. Pour over chicken.','Cover and gently simmer until chicken reaches 165°F in the thickest portion. Avoid vigorous boiling.','Remove chicken, rest briefly and shred or dice. Reduce heat to low and stir cream cheese into the sauce until smooth.','Turn heat off. Stir in Greek yogurt and lime juice; avoid boiling the yogurt. Return chicken to pan and coat thoroughly.','Cool promptly, measure final yield, and fill 1-cup silicone molds. Freeze and transfer solid cubes to labeled bags.'],note:'If your actual yield is not 6 cups, recalculate per-cube macros using total-batch macros ÷ actual number of cups. The sauce may need stirring after reheating.'},
{id:'rice',type:'starch',name:'Restaurant-Style Spanish Rice',tag:'Tomato-forward · fluffy · low fat',desc:'Toasted long-grain rice cooked with tomato, broth, garlic and cumin. Designed to stay flavorful after freezing.',photo:'https://cookingwithcasey.com/assets/images/1742357057450-tytjfy9n.webp',credit:'Cooking with Casey · illustrative',source:'https://cookingwithcasey.com/recipes/restaurant-style-spanish-rice',time:'35–40 min',yield:12,unit:'½ cup',mac:{cal:145,p:3,c:28,f:2},ingredients:[['1.5','cups','dry long-grain white rice'],['1','tbsp','avocado oil'],['0.5','cup','plain tomato sauce'],['2.25','cups','low-sodium chicken broth'],['0.25','','medium yellow onion, finely diced'],['3','','garlic cloves, minced'],['1','tsp','ground cumin'],['0.5','tsp','smoked paprika (optional)'],['0.5','tsp','kosher salt (adjust for broth)'],['0.5','tsp','MSG (optional)'],['1','','bay leaf'],['0.25','cup','finely diced carrots (optional)']],steps:['Heat oil over medium heat. Add dry rice and toast, stirring, for 4–6 minutes until lightly golden.','Add onion and cook 2 minutes; add garlic for 30 seconds.','Add broth, tomato sauce, cumin, optional paprika, salt, MSG and bay leaf. Stir once.','Bring to a boil, cover tightly, reduce heat to low and cook 15–18 minutes or per package instructions.','Turn off heat and rest, covered, 10 minutes. Remove bay leaf and fluff gently.','Spread in a shallow container, refrigerate promptly, then portion into ½-cup molds and freeze.'],note:'Rice yield varies by brand and hydration. Six cups cooked is a planning assumption. For lighter tomato flavor, omit smoked paprika. Rice should not be left cooling at room temperature for hours.'},
{id:'beans',type:'beans',name:'Savory Doctored Refried Beans',tag:'No cheese · creamy · high fiber',desc:'Fast, restaurant-style beans from Rosarita No Fat cans, upgraded with fresh aromatics and warm spices.',photo:'https://images.ctfassets.net/3s5io6mnxfqz/54IFIMZZ9sAvLe9UFWkcMo/ddb491a5d4abc34fdb8b8c877de1d344/refried-beans-recipe.jpeg',credit:'MasterClass · illustrative',source:'https://www.masterclass.com/articles/refried-beans-recipe',time:'15–20 min',yield:8,unit:'½ cup',mac:{cal:95,p:5,c:16,f:1},ingredients:[['2','cans (16 oz each)','Rosarita No Fat Refried Beans'],['0.25–0.5','cup','low-sodium chicken broth, as needed'],['0.25','','medium yellow onion, finely diced'],['2–3','','garlic cloves, minced'],['0–1','tsp','avocado oil (optional; use nonstick pan to omit)'],['0.5','tsp','ground cumin'],['0.25','tsp','smoked paprika'],['0.25','tsp','MSG (optional)'],['1–2','tsp','lime juice'],['1–2','tbsp','diced green chiles (optional)']],steps:['In a nonstick saucepan, soften onion with a splash of broth (or up to 1 tsp oil) for 3–4 minutes.','Add garlic for 30 seconds; stir in cumin and smoked paprika for 15–20 seconds.','Add both cans of beans and ¼ cup broth. Stir until smooth.','Simmer gently for 5–8 minutes, adding more broth in small increments until creamy but scoopable.','Add optional MSG and lime juice, taste before adding salt, and stir through.','Cool promptly, portion into ½-cup molds and freeze. Reheat with a splash of water if needed.'],note:'No cheese. The ~95 kcal target assumes Rosarita No Fat, minimal or no added oil, and roughly 4 cups finished. Confirm the exact can label and measure finished yield.'},
{id:'veggies',type:'vegetable',name:'Roasted Southwest Peppers & Onions',tag:'Fajita-style · colorful · versatile',desc:'A simple medley of bell peppers, poblanos and yellow onion with lightly charred edges. No zucchini or cauliflower.',photo:'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504674900247-0877df9cc836?w=1100&q=85',credit:'Unsplash · illustrative',source:'https://unsplash.com/',time:'30–35 min',yield:6,unit:'½ cup',mac:{cal:45,p:1,c:8,f:2},ingredients:[['1','','red bell pepper'],['1','','yellow bell pepper'],['2','','poblano peppers'],['1','','large yellow onion'],['2','tsp','avocado oil'],['1','tsp','garlic powder'],['0.5','tsp','ground cumin'],['0.5','tsp','smoked paprika'],['','to taste','salt and black pepper'],['','optional','squeeze of lime after roasting']],steps:['Preheat oven to 425°F. Slice peppers and onion into fairly thick, even strips.','Toss vegetables with avocado oil, garlic powder, cumin, smoked paprika, salt and pepper.','Spread in one layer on a large sheet pan; use two pans if crowded.','Roast about 20–25 minutes, turning once, until edges brown but vegetables retain some structure.','Add optional lime, cool promptly and portion into ½-cup molds without extra liquid. Freeze.'],note:'Actual yield depends heavily on pepper and onion sizes and moisture loss. Roasting reduces water, but thawed vegetables will still be softer than fresh.'}
];
const fmt=n=>Number.isInteger(n)?String(n):Number(n.toFixed(2)).toString();function scaleAmount(s,m){if(!s)return '';if(s.includes('–')){let a=s.split('–');return a.map(x=>fmt(Number(x)*m)).join('–')}let n=Number(s);return Number.isFinite(n)?fmt(n*m):s}function makeCard(r){let el=document.createElement('article');el.className='card';el.dataset.text=(r.name+' '+r.tag+' '+r.desc+' '+r.ingredients.map(x=>x[2]).join(' ')+' '+r.type).toLowerCase();el.dataset.type=r.type;el.innerHTML=`<div class="photo"><img src="${r.photo}" loading="lazy" alt="Illustrative photo of ${r.name}" onerror="this.style.display='none'"><a class="credit" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="${r.source}">${r.credit} ↗</a></div><div class="body"><div class="category">${r.type}</div><h2>${r.name}</h2><p class="sub">${r.desc}</p><div class="meta"><span class="pill">⏱ ${r.time}</span><span class="pill">🧊 ${r.unit} per cube</span><span class="pill">~${r.yield} cubes</span></div><div class="macros" id="mac-${r.id}"></div><p class="sub" style="font-size:12px">Estimated per ${r.unit} cube · based on ${r.yield} cubes</p><div class="controls"><label for="yield-${r.id}">Scale recipe to</label><input id="yield-${r.id}" type="number" min="1" max="100" step="1" value="${r.yield}" aria-label="Desired cube count for ${r.name}"><span>${r.unit} cubes</span></div><div class="section"><h3>Ingredients</h3><ul id="ing-${r.id}"></ul></div><div class="section"><h3>Method</h3><ol>${r.steps.map(s=>`<li>${s}</li>`).join('')}</ol></div><div class="note">🧊 <strong>Freezer note:</strong> ${r.note}</div></div>`;return el}function renderIngredients(r){let target=Number(document.getElementById('yield-'+r.id).value)||r.yield;let m=target/r.yield;document.getElementById('ing-'+r.id).innerHTML=r.ingredients.map(([q,u,n])=>`<li>${scaleAmount(q,m)} ${u} ${n}</li>`).join('');document.getElementById('mac-'+r.id).innerHTML=[['cal','kcal'],['p','protein'],['c','carbs'],['f','fat']].map(([k,label])=>`<div class="macro"><strong>${r.mac[k]}${k==='cal'?'':'g'}</strong><small>${label}</small></div>`).join('')}const cards=document.getElementById('cards');recipes.forEach(r=>{cards.append(makeCard(r));document.getElementById('yield-'+r.id).addEventListener('input',()=>renderIngredients(r));renderIngredients(r)});function filter(){let q=document.getElementById('search').value.trim().toLowerCase(),cat=document.getElementById('filter').value,count=0;document.querySelectorAll('.card').forEach(c=>{let yes=c.dataset.text.includes(q)&&(cat==='all'||cat===c.dataset.type);c.style.display=yes?'':'none';count+=yes});document.getElementById('empty').style.display=count?'none':'block'}document.getElementById('search').addEventListener('input',filter);document.getElementById('filter').addEventListener('change',filter);
const builder=document.getElementById('builderItems');recipes.forEach(r=>{let x=document.createElement('div');x.className='build-item';x.innerHTML=`<strong>${r.name}</strong><span class="sub">${r.unit} cube</span><input type="number" id="build-${r.id}" min="0" max="20" step="1" value="${r.id==='chicken'||r.id==='rice'||r.id==='beans'||r.id==='veggies'?1:0}" aria-label="Number of ${r.name} cubes">`;builder.append(x);x.querySelector('input').addEventListener('input',totals)});function totals(){let t={cal:0,p:0,c:0,f:0},cubes=0;recipes.forEach(r=>{let n=Math.max(0,Number(document.getElementById('build-'+r.id).value)||0);cubes+=n;Object.keys(t).forEach(k=>t[k]+=r.mac[k]*n)});document.getElementById('total').innerHTML=`<span><b>${Math.round(t.cal)}</b>calories</span><span><b>${fmt(t.p)}g</b>protein</span><span><b>${fmt(t.c)}g</b>carbs</span><span><b>${fmt(t.f)}g</b>fat</span><span><b>${cubes}</b>total cubes</span>`}totals();function resetAll(){recipes.forEach(r=>{document.getElementById('yield-'+r.id).value=r.yield;renderIngredients(r);document.getElementById('build-'+r.id).value=1});document.getElementById('search').value='';document.getElementById('filter').value='all';filter();totals()}
</script><a href="../index.html" style="position:fixed;bottom:16px;right:16px;background:#203c31;color:white;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:30px;text-decoration:none;font:600 14px system-ui;box-shadow:0 4px 20px #0004;z-index:9999">⌂ Dashboard</a></body></html>
